# Accepted, justified findings -- not hidden, just not blocking.
#
# Every entry here was checked individually via the code-scanning alert's
# own "Fixed Version" field: none of the four have a patched version
# available yet in Debian 12 "bookworm" as of the date noted. Blocking the
# pipeline forever on a CVE nobody can currently patch isn't a quality
# gate, it's a permanently red build -- these are re-evaluated whenever
# this file is touched, and should be removed the moment a fix ships.
#
# Real-world equivalent of what a platform team actually does: document
# and formally accept residual risk for unfixable findings, rather than
# either lowering the severity threshold for everything or leaving the
# build red indefinitely.

# zlib1g 1:1.2.13.dfsg-1 -- CRITICAL, no fix version published (checked
# 2026-08-27). demo-app never decompresses untrusted zlib-compressed data;
# the package is present only as a base-image transitive dependency.
CVE-2023-45853

# libsqlite3-0 3.40.1-2+deb12u2 -- CRITICAL, no fix version published
# (checked 2026-08-27). demo-app has no database and never invokes sqlite3.
CVE-2025-7458

# util-linux-extra 2.38.1-5+deb12u3 -- HIGH, no fix version published
# (checked 2026-08-27). demo-app's container runs as a non-root user and
# never invokes any util-linux binary; these are base-image utilities the
# application itself has no code path that reaches.
CVE-2026-53615
CVE-2026-53613
